{
  "experiment": "independent WSST1 and WSST2 reassignment for each Figure 5 secondary-frequency prior",
  "limitations": [
    "Figure-read priors are approximate and are not tabulated values from the authors.",
    "The paper does not state the GW-spectrum taper. A one-sided end taper is used to avoid suppressing the physical merger onset while conditioning the finite record.",
    "Figure 2 labels the plotted spectrum as post-merger, although the text states that peak extraction uses the full signal including inspiral; secondary dashed lines are therefore taken from Figure 5 rather than redefined from the plotted curve.",
    "Advanced LIGO and Einstein Telescope sensitivity curves from Figure 5 are not overplotted.",
    "Each colored mode is normalized independently, so color intensity cannot compare amplitudes between modes.",
    "Overlapping high-mass priors are deliberately analyzed independently; their ridges are not proof of identifiable physical components.",
    "The composite visualizes separate reassignment results and is not a linear time-domain signal reconstruction."
  ],
  "paper": "Soultanis et al., arXiv:2111.08353v2",
  "prior_provenance": {
    "colors": "Figure 2 convention; purple for the Figure 5 f_spiral-0 addition",
    "dominant_line": "maximum of the full-waveform effective spectrum inside the analytic fpeak drift range",
